        sourceType = "Achievement",
        difficulty = "hard",
        difficultyReason = "Twelve full chapters with rotating / time-gated offers and final hand-ins.",
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Hard - Twelve full chapters with rotating / time-gated offers and final hand-ins.\n\n1. Develop a tier 2 or higher Garrison and use a character eligible for Draenor's level-40 campaign quests. Tier 3 is not required for the original campaign. Inspect the Town Hall, outside noticeboard, visitor NPCs and druid area near the outer gate; trivial-quest tracking helps reveal hidden yellow markers.\n\n2. Finish the first rotating set: The Sargerei at Socrethar's Rise, Darktide Roost, Iron Siegeworks and The Ring of Blood. Accept the Garrison introduction, finish every follow-up and return the final quest. A filled Apexis bonus bar does not finish the story chapter.\n\n3. Finish the second rotating set: The Fall of Shattrath, Bloodmaul Compound, Broken Precipice and Ours is the Fury. The quest routes list the complete follow-ups, including parallel tasks and the final faction-specific hand-in.\n\n4. Complete the final sequence: The Warlord's Council, Heart of the Breakers, A Strike at the Heart, then Primal Fury. For Council, let the captive-cage dialogue finish before taking the escape follow-ups. For Heart of the Breakers, check Choluna / the druids near the Garrison's outer gate if no yellow marker appears on the main map.\n\n5. For Bloodmaul Compound, free the captive, recover the gear, enter the Shadow Gate and finish the soul / totem tasks before placing the totems for Soulgrinder Survivor. For Shattrath, reach the Spire of Light via its flight point, collect the Sargerei Insignia and activate the banner for Socrethar's Demise.\n\n6. For Broken Precipice, recover the three valuables, finish Brokyo and return News for Nixxie. For Primal Fury, finish Awakening at Gorgorek's Rest, then defeat Azuka Bladefury at the Gates of Tanaan in Talador. Do the final hand-in; the later Tanaan Jungle invasion is a separate campaign.\n\n7. If offers stop, resume every partly finished chapter using THIS character's quest flags. Abandoning a quest does not reset the campaign. Revisit that stage's NPC, including Khadgar's Servant for Shattrath, and check beyond the Garrison walls. Once all active work is finished, check again after the next weekly reset; catch-up can sometimes offer another chapter sooner.\n\n8. Confirm all twelve chapter criteria. The six Harrison contracts and 6.2 Tanaan campaign are separate achievements. Don't Call Me Junior currently requires Master Relic Hunter, not this original campaign.",
        stepCount = 8,
        waypoints = {
            { mapID = 590, x = 0.52, y = 0.5, step = 1, label = "Garrison - campaign offers / plots vary" },
