    [9685] = {
        achievementId = 9685,
        name = "Draenor Safari",
        source = "Draenor Safari",
        sourceType = "Achievement",
        difficulty = "medium",
        difficultyReason = "Capture twenty-five specified wild species across six Draenor zones.",
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Medium - Capture twenty-five specified wild species across six Draenor zones.\n\n1. Track Draenor Safari's CURRENT twenty-five named species. Prepare a safe capture attack such as Weakening Blow, healthy backups and bandages. Any quality works; you do not need a rare-quality copy or every wild species added in later patches.\n\n2. Frostfur Rat: Travel to Coldsnap Bluffs, Frostfire Ridge. Search around 54.0,20.2 and the Bloodmaul Slag Mines approach. Rats also accompany Twilight Wasps and other Frostfire pets, so inspect secondary slots instead of waiting for a rare primary. Trap this exact species below 35% health, then win the rest of the battle. Check secondary slots where its individual guide allows backline appearances.\n\n3. Icespine Hatchling: Travel to Frostfire Ridge outside Frostwall and around Grom'gar. Check the long line of larvae near 58,64, then the northern areas around 58,31 and 61.9,15.8. They are ordinary primary encounters, often accompanied by rats and Twilight Wasps. Use the northern locations if the Garrison phase makes nearby pets disappear. Trap this exact species below 35% health, then win the rest of the battle. Check secondary slots where its individual guide allows backline appearances.\n\n4. Twilight Wasp: Travel to Coldsnap Bluffs, Frostfire Ridge. Search around 51.8,20.7 by the Bloodmaul Slag Mines flight point, then the surrounding bluffs near 56,17. These also appear as backlines across Frostfire Ridge. Avoid relying on spawns at Frostwall's phase boundary. Trap this exact species below 35% health, then win the rest of the battle. Check secondary slots where its individual guide allows backline appearances.\n\n5. Frostshell Pincher: Travel to the rocks southeast of Wor'gol, Frostfire Ridge. Search around 23,64 and 24,63 for the few primary crabs. A crab can be inside the rock geometry: target Frostshell Pincher and use Interact With Target from close by. These are primary spawns; searching random backlines is ineffective. Leave the Garrison phase boundary behind. Trap this exact species below 35% health, then win the rest of the battle. Check secondary slots where its individual guide allows backline appearances.\n\n6. Ironclaw Scuttler: Travel to the snowy slopes east of Bladespire Citadel. Take the path up from 34.28,43.15 and sweep north around 33.7,41.4 to 33,38 and 34,35. These primaries are easier to reach on snowy ground than in damaging lava. Stand outside lava before starting; a short lava-protection buff can expire during the battle. Trap this exact species below 35% health, then win the rest of the battle. Check secondary slots where its individual guide allows backline appearances.\n\n7. Moonshell Crab: Travel to Moonlit Shore, north and south of Karabor. Start on the northern beach toward Elodor and follow the waterline around Karabor. Find the crab as a primary; swimming or cliffs can obstruct battles, so stand on dry shore and approach a reachable crab. Do not rely on ordinary Shadowmoon backlines for this species. Trap this exact species below 35% health, then win the rest of the battle. Check secondary slots where its individual guide allows backline appearances.\n\n8. Mossbite Skitterer: Travel to Shadowmoon Valley's Moonlit Shore / Socrethar's Rise. Try the primary spider area at Socrethar's Rise 46.6,77.8. If none are up, move to Moonlit Shore 67.67,34.2 and battle Moonshell Crabs: their backlines can contain this spider. Replies confirm the crab route is useful when the Rise has no visible spiders. Trap this exact species below 35% health, then win the rest of the battle. Check secondary slots where its individual guide allows backline appearances.\n\n9. Zangar Crawler: Travel to Shadowmoon Valley's mushroom beaches and Moonlit Shore. Look on the northern mushroom beaches or battle Moonshell Crabs at 67.67,34.2 for a secondary Zangar Crawler. The Darktide islands are another habitat. An old claim that Horde cannot capture them there was corrected in replies. Trap this exact species below 35% health, then win the rest of the battle. Check secondary slots where its individual guide allows backline appearances.\n\n10. Royal Moth: Travel to Shadowmoon Valley's grassland. Search the grass and woods for primary moths and inspect other local pet teams. Talador is another habitat if you are already collecting there. Royal Moth is distinct from Talador's scarce Crimsonwing Moth; use the journal name to tell them apart. Trap this exact species below 35% health, then win the rest of the battle. Check secondary slots where its individual guide allows backline appearances.\n\n11. Waterfly: Travel to Shadowmoon Valley's waterways. Follow pools and stream edges and check secondary slots in local wild battles. Talador and Tanaan Jungle provide additional habitats. Stand on shore to avoid obstructed-area errors; Waterfly is a Flying pet despite its aquatic habitat. Trap this exact species below 35% health, then win the rest of the battle. Check secondary slots where its individual guide allows backline appearances.\n\n12. Wood Wasp: Travel to Ruins of the First Bastion, southern Gorgrond. Look near 50.49,80.26 for a primary wasp. If none is reachable, battle Junglebeaks, Axebeak Hatchlings, Parched Lizards or local frogs and inspect their backlines; comments report Wood Wasps throughout Gorgrond as secondary pets. Trap this exact species below 35% health, then win the rest of the battle. Check secondary slots where its individual guide allows backline appearances.\n\n13. Amberbarb Wasp: Travel to southern Gorgrond's jungle. Search the jungle for green-paw wasps and inspect secondary slots in other local wild fights. Amberbarb, Twilight and Wood Wasp share a general model but are separate species; confirm the name before throwing your one trap. Trap this exact species below 35% health, then win the rest of the battle. Check secondary slots where its individual guide allows backline appearances.\n\n14. Junglebeak: Travel to Gorgrond's southern jungle and Broken Horn Village. Look for primary birds or battle Wood Wasps and other jungle pets for a backline Junglebeak. Some primaries hover above awkward terrain and fail to start a battle; use a reachable bird or the backline route instead of repeatedly clicking a broken spawn. Trap this exact species below 35% health, then win the rest of the battle. Check secondary slots where its individual guide allows backline appearances.\n\n15. Axebeak Hatchling: Travel to Gorgrond's jungle and Broken Horn Village. Search for primary hatchlings and inspect Junglebeak, Wood Wasp and Twilight Wasp teams. Comments also report backlines near the Iron Docks. Choose another battle if a bird is stuck too far above the ground. Trap this exact species below 35% health, then win the rest of the battle. Check secondary slots where its individual guide allows backline appearances.\n\n16. Mudback Calf: Travel to the Fertile Ground and Tailthrasher Basin, Gorgrond. Check the water edges at 41,77 and 45,90 for a primary calf. Move your character onto clear dry land if the battle is obstructed. Later replies report more visible spawns in War Mode, but it is an optional alternate shard with PvP enabled, not a guaranteed spawn trigger. Ordinary non-battle calves cannot be trapped. Trap this exact species below 35% health, then win the rest of the battle. Check secondary slots where its individual guide allows backline appearances.\n\n17. Brilliant Bloodfeather: Travel to Talador, including the country around Vol'jin's Pride. Search the woodland and grass around the northern Talador settlements. Local Bloodfeather battles around 72,22 can also supply Kelp Scuttlers in the backline. Confirm Brilliant Bloodfeather rather than the similar Golden Dawnfeather from Spires. Trap this exact species below 35% health, then win the rest of the battle. Check secondary slots where its individual guide allows backline appearances.\n\n18. Kelp Scuttler: Travel to the northern Talador coast and Shattrath shoreline. Start on the beach around 54,18. Check dry sand rather than trying to start while swimming in Shattrath Harbor. It can also be secondary to Brilliant Bloodfeather near 72,22 or other Talador coastal pets. Trap this exact species below 35% health, then win the rest of the battle. Check secondary slots where its individual guide allows backline appearances.\n\n19. Flat-Tooth Calf: Travel to Duskfall Lake and the rivers toward Auchindoun, Talador. Sweep the banks at 64,55 and 68,62, then south to 58,74 and 55.8,81.8. Find its own green-paw primary. Reports confirm captures throughout the day; neither a particular clock time nor carrying Arrowbloom is a demonstrated requirement. Trap this exact species below 35% health, then win the rest of the battle. Check secondary slots where its individual guide allows backline appearances.\n\n20. Shadow Sporebat: Travel to Zangarra's ravine, caves and ledges, Talador. Check 84,31 by Khadgar's Tower, the cave around 80,30 and the ledges around 80.9,27.7. Descend into the ravine: minimap paws can be hidden when you stay high by the flight point. Check the caves visually. Reports from both daytime and dry weather contradict a night/rain requirement. Capture the first quality you find. Trap this exact species below 35% health, then win the rest of the battle. Check secondary slots where its individual guide allows backline appearances.\n\n21. Thicket Skitterer: Travel to central Spires of Arak, southeast of Axefall. Search the undergrowth near 45.0,47.3, southeast of Axefall. Check low vegetation and nearby wild-pet teams for the spider. The hostile ravagers and ordinary spider critters cannot be trapped. Trap this exact species below 35% health, then win the rest of the battle. Check secondary slots where its individual guide allows backline appearances.\n\n22. Bloodsting Wasp: Travel to southern Spires of Arak between Southport and Pinchwhistle. Search southeast of Axefall and near 48,65 west of Bloodmane Valley. Visible primary wasps can be sparse: sweep the road and vegetation toward Pinchwhistle rather than waiting at one point. Secure any quality and use a stone later. Trap this exact species below 35% health, then win the rest of the battle. Check secondary slots where its individual guide allows backline appearances.\n\n23. Golden Dawnfeather: Travel to the forests around Southport and Axefall, Spires of Arak. Check 44,61 and 58,68. The small birds without a green paw are ordinary critters. Some outpost boundaries phase primaries out: use another spawn away from the boundary. Its Love Potion heals it; reduce its health again before trapping rather than assuming the old health total still applies. Trap this exact species below 35% health, then win the rest of the battle. Check secondary slots where its individual guide allows backline appearances.\n\n24. Swamplighter Firefly: Travel to Spires of Arak's coasts. Begin near Pinchwhistle Point at 54.5,87.3 and follow the coast toward Pinchwhistle Gearworks and Lost Veil Anzu. Check the western Writhing Mire if the east coast is empty. Ordinary decorative fireflies do not replace the green-paw encounter. Trap this exact species below 35% health, then win the rest of the battle. Check secondary slots where its individual guide allows backline appearances.\n\n25. Leatherhide Runt: Travel to the plains and Hallvalor, Draenor Nagrand. Follow clefthoof herds across the plains near 70,56. These are primary pets, not ordinary backline companions. Check the hut with cages at Hallvalor 85,55; if a capturable runt is behind a cage, try an adjacent open stall or another angle. Use the open plains if the battle area is obstructed. Trap this exact species below 35% health, then win the rest of the battle. Check secondary slots where its individual guide allows backline appearances.\n\n26. Mud Jumper: Travel to Draenor Nagrand's rivers and fungal grove. Follow riverbanks and lake outlets, including the northern mushroom grove. Ordinary frogs without paws are not battle pets. Mud Jumpers also occur in Talador and Spires of Arak; inspect local aquatic battles if you are already collecting there. Trap this exact species below 35% health, then win the rest of the battle. Check secondary slots where its individual guide allows backline appearances.\n\n27. Check all twenty-five criteria, then collect and learn the Royal Peacock/Royal Peachick reward. Crimsonwing Moth, Sapphire Firefly and later Tanaan species are NOT extra criteria in the current tooltip; older all-pets routes can overstate this achievement.",
        stepCount = 27,
        waypoints = {
            { mapID = 525, x = 0.54, y = 0.20199999999999999, step = 2, label = "Coldsnap Bluffs - rats and wasp backlines" },
